    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSeptember 25th - Bidding concluded. Reserved subject to Contracts being signed.\n\n \n\nA beautiful Apartment with an enclosed outside space for the exclusive use of the new Owner, is now available. Located within a gated development of only 29 units, this Apartment is ideally suited to an Owner-occupier looking for a mature setting with an easy walk to all local services in Blessington Town.\n\n20 The Tramway is an appealing Apartment located on the ground floor and benefiting from its own garden, which attracts an ideal South-westerly aspect and has independent rear access. The Apartment is very well presented, requiring little investment after purchase and has natural gas central heating. Containing two double Bedrooms and one Bathroom, it is the living area which is surprisingly well proportioned, with ample space for dining and living plus a cosy TV snug. The Kitchen is well equipped with floor and eye-level units, and all appliances are included in the sale. Outside, the enclosed garden is a massive bonus, particularly because of its orientation - natural light from early morning to later in the evening, and surprisingly both Bedrooms have direct access into the garden area.\n\nThe Tramway is an early 2000's development of solid construction and an attractive brick and napp plaster finish. Offering ample parking space and a communal green area with very mature shrubbery, the development has the rare bonus of external communal storage space x 2. Located just off Main Street, The Tramway development is a short walk from Blessington Town Centre, local churches, local community clubs and services. An excellent development for the Owner-occupier, but also an excellent investment (open market rent will apply to a new tenancy). Blessington is served with regular public bus routes to Dublin City (No.65 and 132) and more recently the Local Link gives access to Naas Town and to Salins Rail Station. The LUAS Red Line is available at nearby Tallaght. \n\nNo 20 The Tramway is suited to 1st-time Buyers or to persons who intend downsizing. Easy access to employment centres in City West Business Campus, Sandyford Business Park and Naas Town will underpin future resaleability. A vibrant community on your doorstep yet a tranquil living environment immediately around you. An ideal opportunity to secure a base in the prosperous town of Blessington and to enjoy the wide range of amenities, clubs and outdoor pursuits on one's doorstep.\n\nIMMEDIATE VIEWING IS STRONGLY RECOMMENDED. Contact REA Murphy for your appointment.\n\n \n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nEntrance Hall.\n\nLiving and Dining area.\n\nKitchen.\n\nBathroom.\n\n2 Double Bedrooms.\n\n \n\nOUTSIDE:\n\nPrivate rear garden with rear access.\n\nCommunal gardens.\n\nAllocated parking for 1 car visitor parking available.\n\nCommunal storage x 2.\n\n \n\nSERVICES:\n\nNatural gas central heating.\n\nElectricity.\n\nExcellent internet.\n\nPublic transport.\n\nAnnual management charge: 1333 for 2026.\n\nLOCATION:\n\nCity West Business Park 16Km Sandyford Business Park 20Km Naas Town 13Km\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Quality ground floor Apartment with its own garden space.\nSouth-west facing, sun-drenched outdoor space. \nGated community of only 29 units with added privacy and security.\nBeautifully mature development.\nEasy walking distance to Blessington Town Centre and to local services and amenities.\nWalk-in condition with contents included (optional).\nIdeally suited to 1st time Buyer or 'trading-down' Buyer.\nStrong investment opportunity with 'open-market' rent available."
